    <GaugingStation location="Craighall" name="Ericht" number="15025">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Velocity area station gauging a natural catchment. Ice build up can occur at the station.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Cableway present. All flows contained, rating curve well defined. Multiple peak flow ratings across period of record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Velocity area station, 46m wide. Stable bedrock control. Station added to peak flows dataset in August 2024 (WINFAP Files v13).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Extreme low temperatures can cause ice build up and hence erroneous flow values, e.g. Dec 2001 - Jan 2002.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Flows are natural.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Mountainous steeply sloping catchment. Mostly impermeable bedrock, metamorphic, two thirds overlain by superficial deposits. Land use mainly rough grazing with some forestry.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">N</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Rating well supported by gaugings to QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Flows are contained and the rating is informed by flood gaugings." suitable="Yes" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
